Publicly, to prime count given limit as a whole number, named prime_count, giving a whole number.
Let count be 0.
Let n be 2.
While n is at most limit.
Let prime be 1.
Let d be 2.
While d times d is at most n.
If n modulo d equals 0.
Set prime to 0.
Break.
End the condition.
Add 1 to d.
End the loop.
If prime equals 1, add 1 to count.
Add 1 to n.
End the loop.
Give back count.
